A lot of people try one sec, like the idea, and then notice their thumb learns to skip the pause. The research agrees: in the PNAS study, the share of attempts people abandoned fell from 43% in week one to about 32-34% from week three.

The same paper found the option to back out was the active ingredient, and the 10-second wait added nothing beyond it. A separate CHI 2024 study of 1,039 users found use rebounded after breaks from the friction.

We compared ScreenZen, ClearSpace, Pause Point, Opal, Brick and Screen Time with prices checked from their own listings. DeRot makes an app in this space, so it isn't ranked. {url}
